{"id":"congo-nile-trail","title":"Congo Nile Trail","who":"Classic route · Rwanda along Lake Kivu by bike","when":"June to September and December to February (drier)","vehicle":"Mountain or gravel bike, 5–7 days","kind":"bike","color":"#15803d","summary":"About 230–260 km along the shore of Lake Kivu, from Rubavu to Rusizi on the border with the DR Congo: red dirt roads over endless steep hills of tea, coffee and banana, with a lot of climbing and children running alongside. Guesthouses and lake beaches at the ends of the days.","sources":[{"label":"Bikepacking.com: the Congo Nile Trail (bikepacker's edition)","url":"https://bikepacking.com/routes/congo-nile-trail/"},{"label":"Afar: five days biking Rwanda's Congo Nile Trail","url":"https://www.afar.com/magazine/what-its-like-biking-rwandas-congo-nile-trail"},{"label":"Pro Cycling UK: cycling the Congo Nile Trail, stages and advice","url":"https://procyclinguk.com/cycling-in-congo-nile-trail/"}],"approximate":"The usual stages; the line follows tracks near the marked trail.","km":221,"bbox":[28.9088,-2.4872,29.4109,-1.6933],"stops":[{"name":"Rubavu (Gisenyi)","place":"Gisenyi, Rwanda","at":[-1.6935,29.2599],"text":"A lakeside town with a beach, facing Goma across the border.","photo":{"url":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/GisenyiBeach.jpg/500px-GisenyiBeach.jpg","page":"Gisenyi","source":"https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:GisenyiBeach.jpg","credit":"No machine-readable author provided. Amakuru assumed (based on copyright claims).","license":"CC BY-SA 3.0"}},{"name":"Kinunu","place":"Kinunu, Rwanda","at":[-1.9547,29.3036],"text":"Up and down the first steep hills to a coffee washing station by the lake.","source":{"label":"Bikepacking.com route","url":"https://bikepacking.com/routes/congo-nile-trail/"}},{"name":"Karongi (Kibuye)","place":"Kibuye, Rwanda","at":[-2.0604,29.3486],"text":"Islands and peninsulas on the lake, and a memorial to remember 1994."},{"name":"Nyamasheke","place":"